          "path": "_m/g/c/k/v/criccieth-wp/capel-y-traeth-criccie.jpg",
          "filename": "Criccieth - Capel Seion.JPG",
          "caption": "Capel y Traeth, Criccieth. Capel y Traeth on Penpaled Road has a notable porticoed façade. It was built at a cost of £2,040 in 1895 by Owen Roberts of Porthmadog. Previously known as Capel Seion, it was renamed in 1995 when the congregation merged with that of Capel Mawr, reuniting the two congregations that had separated in 1889.",
